  "notes": "Grundig Android UHD TV (Arcelik-built, codename \"kunyang\", product GxGrNM), Turkey\nAndroid TV 14 (API 34), build UKNV.260115.001, MediaTek, 1.8 GB RAM, UI 1920x1080 on a 4K panel.\nro.product.manufacturer = ARCELIK, ro.adb.secure = 1. USB debugging alone opens port 5555.\n\nApply:   TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/disable.sh examples/grundig-kunyang/debloat.txt\nUndo:    TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/restore.sh examples/grundig-kunyang/debloat.txt\nEverything is DISABLED, not uninstalled. Comment out any line you want to keep.\n\nStock launcher: com.google.android.tvlauncher (classic Android TV home, not Google TV launcherx).\nsetupwraith does NOT claim HOME on this build, so it stays enabled (it also owns a saved Wi-Fi network).\n\nKEEP, even though the names look like bloat (checked with dumpsys package, none of them started):\n- fusion.android.tv.demo: answers android.intent.action.TV_INPUT_BUTTON, i.e. the remote's Input key.\n- com.arcelik.smartremoteservice: GLOBAL_BUTTON receiver and remote server (remote keys).\n- com.mediatek.autopair (persistent): Bluetooth remote pairing.\n- com.arcelik.tv.arcelikbacklight (persistent): backlight control service.\n- com.mediatek.android.leanbacklauncher.partnercustomizer: crash-loops tv.service on MediaTek when off\n(see examples/cecotec-shandao, same Turkish Android 14 platform family).\n- com.mediatek.tv.service, com.mediatek.tvinput, com.mediatek.wwtv.tvcenter: Live TV, HDMI, source menu.\n- com.arcelik.ChannelEditor, .ecomode, .picturecustomizer, .ToneMaster, .easy_installation: TV settings.\n- Factory packages, never opened: arcelik.factory.factorystart, com.mediatek.tv.factory,\nmediatek.factorymenu.ui, com.arcelik.tv.rctest.\n\nReboot-checked: pm list packages -d identical before and after; nothing is re-enabled at boot.\nLauncher works: installs over pm install (no verifier), owns Home (mFocusedApp) also after reboot;\nevery remote button (Home, Input, Settings, app keys) works without the key services. Live TV is\ncom.mediatek.wwtv.tvcenter. Screensaver set to com.gathin.tvhome/.ClockDream before backdrop goes.\nPrivate DNS works on this set.\n\nOwner's choices: Chromecast and YouTube Music kept; voice assistant, AirScreen/AirCast,\nYouTube Kids, Play Movies and Play Games off. Self-installed streaming apps untouched.\n--- Telemetry, analytics and install attribution",
